<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bodawpaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1819">1819</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bodawpaya was the sixth king of the Konbaung dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, reigning from 1782 to 1819. He conquered the kingdom of Arakan in 1784 to 1785, carrying the revered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahamuni-buddha">Mahamuni Buddha</a> image to his capital, and made costly failed invasions of Siam. His annexations brought Burma into contact with British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, setting the stage for the Anglo-Burmese wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bodawpaya.jpg" alt="Bodawpaya" width="320" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kantabon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statute_of_king_Bodawpaya_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
